# RAG — Blog semantic assistant

Hybrid retrieval (pgvector + `tsvector` + RRF) over published posts, with local BGE-M3 embeddings and Groq `openai/gpt-oss-20b` for answers. Follows the standard module layout (domain → application → infrastructure).

## Chunking

- Always strip Markdown with `remove-markdown` before chunking (`IndexPostUseCase`).
- Target size: 200–1500 characters (`CHUNK_MIN_CHARS` / `CHUNK_MAX_CHARS`), with 100 characters of overlap (`CHUNK_OVERLAP_CHARS`).
- Prefer paragraph boundaries (`\n\n`). Split oversized text at the last `.` / `?` / `!` before the max length.
- Constants live in `application/constants/chunking.constants.ts`.

## Embedding

- Never instantiate the `@xenova/transformers` pipeline outside `EmbeddingService`.
- Before `pipeline()`, set `env.cacheDir` from `ConfigService` (`EMBEDDINGS_CACHE_DIR`) when that variable is present. The image sets it to `/var/cache/johnish-api/embeddings`. Compose mounts the named volume `johnish_api_embeddings_cache` there so BGE-M3 is not downloaded again on each image build. Do not bake the download into the Docker build and do not cache weights inside `node_modules`.
- Document chunks: `embedDocument(text)` — **no** instruction prefix.
- Search queries: `embedQuery(query)` — always uses `BGE_QUERY_PREFIX` from `infrastructure/utils/embedding.constants.ts`.
- If the pipeline is not initialized, throw `ServiceUnavailableException`.

## LLM (Groq)

- Every Groq call goes through `GroqService.generateAnswer()`.
- Model and retries: `GROQ_MODEL`, `GROQ_MAX_RETRIES` in `infrastructure/utils/groq.constants.ts`.
- Use `temperature: 0`.
- The system prompt must constrain the model to answer only from the provided context (`RAG_SYSTEM_PROMPT`).
- Only `GroqService` maps Groq/API errors. Use cases receive either a string answer or `ServiceUnavailableException` — never handle Groq network/rate-limit details themselves.

## Hybrid search

- All vector + FTS retrieval uses the RRF SQL in `PostChunkRepositoryImpl.hybridSearch()`.
- Do not run semantic and FTS searches separately outside the repository.
- Scope to `published = true` inside each CTE leg.
- `RAG_TOP_K` (default 5) is the final limit; candidate limit per leg is 50 (keep in sync with the SQL `LIMIT 50` / `RAG_CANDIDATE_LIMIT` docs).

## Indexing events

Event names follow `post.<action>`:

| Event              | When                                        | Handler              |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------- | -------------------- |
| `post.published`   | Draft → published only (idempotent publish) | `IndexPostUseCase`   |
| `post.updated`     | Saved post is published                     | `IndexPostUseCase`   |
| `post.unpublished` | Was published before unpublish              | `UnindexPostUseCase` |

- Payload is always `{ postId: string }`.
- Listeners (`PostIndexingListener`) only call use cases — never repositories directly.
- Post delete relies on DB `ON DELETE CASCADE` for `posts_chunks`; no listener required.

## Ask flow (`AskBlogUseCase`)

- If `hybridSearch` returns empty: return `RAG_NO_MATCH_ANSWER` with `sources: []` and **do not** call the LLM.
- Never pass an empty context to Groq.
- `sources` are derived from `[n]` citations in the LLM answer, mapped to the numbered retrieval chunks (1-based). Out-of-range indices are ignored; deduplicate by `postId`. If the answer has no citations, return `sources: []`.

## HTTP

- Public endpoint: `POST /api/rag/ask` (no auth guard).
- Controller only delegates to `AskBlogUseCase` and wraps with `ApiResponseDto.ok`.
